From ccbd1768b3e8bf29fb81cf3a82b1c21509009b68 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: MoeLeak <i@leak.moe>
Date: Mon, 12 Oct 2026 21:17:39 +0800
Subject: [PATCH] test(sidebar): make config watcher test independent of OS
 event latency

project_config_watcher_recovers_registration_and_directory_replacement
drove the real notify backend and expected each event within 5s, using
700ms sleeps to wait for watch registration. On macOS the backend is
FSEvents, whose events go through the system-wide fseventsd. When the
rest of the test suite (or anything else on the machine) churns files,
fseventsd falls behind: delivery lags 14s during a full local test run
and 50s+ under heavier load. The test then times out, which breaks
`nix build` of the package on macOS.

Make spawn_config_watcher generic over the notify::Watcher backend
(production still uses RecommendedWatcher). Drive the test with an
in-process fake watcher that binds each watch to the directory's
identity, like inotify/kqueue, and wait on registration state instead
of sleeping. The test still fails if a missing directory is never
retried, if a replaced directory is not re-watched, or if dropping a
project unwatches the shared global config directory. Event-kind
handling, including atomic renames, stays covered by the
config_event_triggers_reload unit tests.
